goc: Bellard QuickJS 2026-06-04 on moving goroutine stacks (QJS_FLAVOR=bellard).
Applied by scripts/qjs-build.sh to third_party/quickjs-bellard (pristine
https://bellard.org/quickjs/quickjs-2026-06-04.tar.xz). Everything is under
#ifdef GOC_QJS_GSTACK, so a native build of the patched tree is unchanged.
 - quickjs.c js_check_stack_overflow: measure depth from the current
   g.stack.hi (same as scripts/qjs-gstack.patch for quickjs-ng).
 - quickjs.c JS_AtomGetStrRT: the pure-ASCII fast path copies into the
   caller's buffer instead of returning the atom's heap bytes (a function
   returning either a stack buffer or a heap pointer is rejected by the goc
   escape check). Names longer than 63 bytes are truncated in the messages
   that use it, as Bellard already does for non-ASCII names.
 - libregexp.c lre_exec_backtrack: identical to the quickjs-ng hunks (saved
   pointers decoded from uptr words, loop counters kept out of capture[]).

